{"availability":"available","full":"e-m-b-a/emba","name":"emba","description":"EMBA - The firmware security analyzer","category":"Developer tools","language":"Shell","stars":3696,"forks":335,"created":"2020-08-25T07:59:12Z","updated":"2026-10-09T16:47:59Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://www.securefirmware.de","topics":["artificial-intelligence","binary-analysis","embedded-linux","embedded-systems","firmware","firmware-analysis","firmware-tools","hacking","infosec","iot","linux","penetration-testing","pentesting","reverse-engineering","sbom","security","security-tools","static-analyzer","vulnerability-scanner","vulnerability-scanners"],"demo":"https://www.securefirmware.de/emba/index.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:29.631Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:29.631Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:29.631Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:29.631Z","stars":3696,"forks":335}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["EMBA is designed as the central firmware analysis and SBOM tool for penetration testers, product security teams, developers and responsible product managers. It supports the complete security analysis process starting with firmware extraction, doing static analysis and dynamic analysis via emulation, building the SBOM and finally generating a web based vulnerability report. EMBA automatically discovers possible weak spots and vulnerabilities in firmware. Examples are insecure binaries, old and outdated software components, potentially vulnerable scripts, or hard-coded passwords. EMBA is a…","EMBA assists the penetration testers, product security teams and developers in the identification of weak spots and vulnerabilities in the firmware image. EMBA provides as much information as possible about the firmware, that the tester can decide on focus areas and is responsible for verifying and interpreting the results."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://gith